    "probe_text": "Read the whole pipeline. Here is every validation and side-effect for `POST /api/owners`, in the order it actually runs.\n\n## Precondition (whole endpoint)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml` has `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. The caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` or the request is rejected before any step runs.\n\nAll steps below (except the two validation steps and the responders) run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so persistence commits once at the end of the pipeline.\n\n## 1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`\n\n- Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header directly off the connection (missing \u2192 `null`, not a 400).\n- **Side-effect:** publishes the key (possibly `null`) as a variable for step 19.\n- **Branch:** if the key was seen before *and* the recorded owner still exists and is not soft-deleted, it takes the `existing` flow \u2192 `RespondWithExistingOwner` (200, the original owner) and **the entire create pipeline below is skipped** (no duplicate created). A missing/blank/unknown key falls through to a normal create.\n\n*(`RespondWithExistingOwner`, on the replay path only, re-derives `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `riskFlag` onto the DTO and returns it with 200.)*\n\n## 2. `ValidateOwnerFields` (the only `@RequestBody` reader)\n\nIn this internal order:\n- Normalizes the address via `AddressNormalizer` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` are preferred; the flat `address` is the fallback.\n- **Validation:** required-field check on `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (blank *after* normalization), `city`, `telephone`. Any missing/blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400, `errors` array).\n- **Side-effect:** writes normalized `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and the composed `address` back onto the body.\n- Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 via `TelephoneE164` (strips separators, assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0` when no country code; enforces 8\u201315 digits and country-code-specific national length). **Validation:** un-normalizable \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400). **Side-effect:** stores the E.164 telephone.\n- Normalizes `email` via `OwnerEmail` (optional). If present: **validation** it must be syntactically valid \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400), and its domain must not be a blocklisted disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400). **Side-effect:** stores it lower-cased.\n- **Side-effect:** republishes the validated body for later steps.\n\n## 3. `ValidatePostcode`\n\n- **Validation (postcode optional):** if present it must be 4 digits \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400); if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Unknown city accepts any 4-digit value.\n\n## 4. `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`\n\n- **Validation:** if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n\n## 5. `EnsureCityCapacity`\n\n- **Validation:** counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409). Count excludes the owner being created (the 51st is the first rejected).\n\n## 6. `ResolveRegistrationDate`\n\n- **Side-effect:** computes the effective registration date = supplied date, else today; rolls weekends/public holidays forward to the next business day (`BusinessDay`); publishes it as a variable.\n\n## 7. `EnsureDailyCapacity`\n\n- **Validation:** counts existing owners already registered on that business-day-adjusted date; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyLimitException` (429).\n\n## 8. `BuildOwner`\n\n- **Side-effect:** maps the validated body into a new `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper`) and sets its registration date to the resolved business-day date.\n\n## 9. `AssignHousehold`\n\n- **Side-effect:** computes a deterministic `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName | postcode | identityRegion)` and sets it on the owner (in place).\n\n## 10. `EnsureUniqueIdentity`\n\n- **Validation:** compares the owner's derived `identityKey` (`SHA-256(normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName))`) against all non-deleted existing owners; an exact match \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## 11. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`\n\n- **Side-effect:** unless `sharesHousehold: true`, flags a soft/phonetic near-match (same Soundex last name + same postcode, different identity key) by setting `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest matching owner id.\n\n## 12. `AssignHouseholdMemberCount`\n\n- **Side-effect:** sets `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing the `householdId` + 1 (1 when no household id).\n\n## 13. `AssignMemberId`\n\n- **Side-effect:** sets `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><Luhn>`, appending `-<n>` (n\u22652) on collision with an existing member id.\n\n## 14. `AssignNamesakeCount`\n\n- **Side-effect:** sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## 15. `CapMembershipLevel`\n\n- **Side-effect:** unless `sharesHousehold: true`, sets `membershipLevelCap` = (max membership level among existing non-deleted household members) + 1, when the household has any existing member.\n\n## 16. `SaveOwner`\n\n- **Side-effect:** `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists the owner (id assigned).\n\n## 17. `AuditOwnerCreated`\n\n- **Side-effect:** logs to the `AUDIT` logger \u2014 a human-readable line, then a structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON (stamping a process-wide monotonic sequence number).\n\n## 18. `EnqueueWelcomeNotification`\n\n- **Side-effect:** logs a welcome line to the `NOTIFY` logger with the owner id and `memberId`.\n\n## 19. `RecordIdempotencyKey`\n\n- **Side-effect:** records the new owner's id against the request's idempotency key in the `IdempotencyStore` (no-op when no key was supplied), enabling future replay in step 1.\n\n## 20. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n\n- **Side-effect (response-only):** maps to `OwnerDto` and derives three response flags \u2014 `bulkSignupWarning` (>80 owners today), `capacityWarning` (city at 40\u201349), `riskFlag` (possible-duplicate OR disposable-adjacent email OR city over soft-cap). Sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\nNote: the required-field, postcode, future-date, telephone and email checks are all **400s**; city capacity and duplicate identity are **409s**; daily limit is **429**. The `bulkSignupWarning`/`capacityWarning`/`riskFlag` values are computed fresh at response time and are not persisted state changes."
